  "summary": "Buffer overflow with AES key wrap with padding in `cipher_update_inplace`",
  "details": "`CipherCtxRef::cipher_update_inplace` had the same sizing error that 0.10.79 fixed in `cipher_update` (GHSA-xv59-967r-8726); that fix missed this method. It required room for `inlen + block_size` bytes, but with the AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers OpenSSL writes up to 7 more bytes when `inlen` is not a multiple of 8, past the end of `data`.\n\nOnly users of the AES key-wrap-with-padding ciphers are affected. `cipher_update_inplace` was added in 0.10.50, and 0.10.80 applies the corrected size check to it.",
